  "@type": "AnalogicalMapping",
  "instance_name": "onion_chopping_discomfort_mapping",
  "label": "The person's discomfort is mapped onto the act of chopping onions",
  "description": "The visual of the person making a face of discomfort with hands framing their eyes is mapped onto the textual description 'when you chop onions'. This creates an analogical mapping where the person's physical reaction (discomfort) is understood as a direct consequence of the mundane kitchen task (chopping onions). The mapping is based on the universal biological phenomenon of onion-induced eye irritation, which makes the visual expression relatable and humorous in the context of the text. The person in the image serves as a visual proxy for anyone experiencing this common, irritating situation.",
